/*
 * zakfix.mjs
 *
 * Ye ek script pichhli do (zakcart.mjs, zakname.mjs) ki jagah leti hai -
 * unme se koi chalayi ho ya na chalayi ho, sirf yahi chala do.
 *
 * Four things the messages were getting wrong.
 *
 * 1. The abandoned-cart reminder said "your item". The webhook stored only
 *    how many lines the cart had, never the names, so hours later there was
 *    nothing to say. Now the product line is written down with the cart.
 *
 * 2. The product name was a whole shop title cut off at 46 characters with
 *    three dots on the end. On a phone that reads like the message broke.
 *    Now it is the one or two words that name the thing, and no message
 *    ever ends in dots:
 *
 *      Kids Portable LCD Writing Tablet for Drawing   ->  Writing Tablet
 *      2-in-1 Mini Bag Sealer and Cutter - USB        ->  Bag Sealer
 *      Car Vacuum Cleaner 120W High Power             ->  Vacuum Cleaner
 *      Stainless Steel Water Bottle 1L                ->  Water Bottle
 *      Portable Blender                               ->  Portable Blender
 *
 * 3. The reminder's button opened the shop front instead of the cart.
 *    Shopify only sometimes fills in a recovery URL, and when it did not
 *    the link had nowhere to go. The variant ids are now written down with
 *    the cart, so the link rebuilds it: /cart/<id>:<qty>,... - same items,
 *    straight to the cart.
 *
 * 4. Stray spaces. Every value is squeezed to single spaces and trimmed
 *    before it goes to Meta, so a space can never open a gap in a message.
 *
 * Every file it touches is copied to ..\zak-bak first, and a file that is
 * not the version this script was built against is left alone and named.
 * Run it from the repo root.
 */

import { readFileSync, writeFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, copyFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { join, dirname } from "node:path";
import { createHash } from "node:crypto";

